# Belt-and-braces over the root .gitignore's `config/.env` and
# `config/config.yaml`. A second rule costs nothing and survives someone
# tidying the root file; a leaked credential does not survive anything.
.env
*.env
config.yaml

# NOT `*.yaml`. config/agents/ holds three TRACKED agent definitions, so a
# blanket rule is already contradicted by the directory's own contents -- and
# because git never un-tracks a file an ignore rule catches late, the three
# would keep working while the NEXT agent added here vanished silently. An
# ignore rule that is wrong about tracked files is invisible until it eats an
# untracked one.
